WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.602
Welcome back to State of the Union.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.770
Former President Trump

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.505
is attempting to defend a meal

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.406
he shared this week

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.107
with rapper

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:10.410
Kanye West, who now goes by Jay and white

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.412
nationalist and Holocaust denier

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.446
Nick Fuentes.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.015
Trump insisted Friday that he hadn't

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.616
previously known Fuentes,

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.884
but a source tells CNN

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.519
he found the white supremacist

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.820
quote, very interesting,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.655
particularly fantasies, ability

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:23.323
to rattle off

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:24.824
statistics and data

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.893
and his familiarity with Trump.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.261
Here with me

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.629
now is Arkansas

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.464
Republican Governor Asa Hutchinson,

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.432
who is considering

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.034
challenging Donald Trump

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.836
for the 2024 GOP nomination.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.170
Governor,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.172
thank you so much for joining me.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.741
I know as US attorney in Arkansas,

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.877
you personally prosecuted

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.745
white supremacist groups.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:46.546
What's your reaction

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.148
to seeing a former US president

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.083
associate with someone like that?

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.454
Well, I hope someday we won't

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.523
have to be responding to what

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.492
former President Trump has said or done.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:00.827
In this instance,

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.429
it's important to respond.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.329
And as you mentioned,

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.331
the last time I met with a

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:06.499
white supremacist,

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.101
it was in an armed standoff.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.537
I had a bulletproof vest on.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:11.805
We arrested them,

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:14.174
prosecuted him and sent them to prison.

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.008
And so, no,

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.476
I don't think it's a good idea

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.344
for a leader

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.814
that's setting an example for the country

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:21.481
or the party

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.249
to meet with avowed

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.285
racist or anti-Semite.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.454
And so it's very troubling

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:29.189
and it shouldn't happen.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.624
And we need to avoid those kinds

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.560
of empowering the extremes.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.861
And when you meet with people,

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.296
you empower,

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:38.264
and that's what you have to avoid.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.166
You want to diminish their strength,

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.568
not empower them.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.336
Stay away from.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.305
Trump has released multiple statements.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.507
What he's doing is he's denying knowing

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:48.675
Nick Fuentes,

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.610
but he's not condemning his views.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.811
Let alone condemning

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:52.779
Kanye West's

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.914
history of anti-Semitic comments,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.150
recent history. So it's a pattern

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.121
Well,

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:01.721
I mean, you can

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:02.889
have accidental meetings,

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:04.157
things like that happen.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.859
This was not an accidental meeting.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.727
It was a set up

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.597
dinner with Kanye.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.966
And so this happened.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:15.668
But you certainly have every occasion

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.204
that the question of white supremacy

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.340
or neo-Nazi ism

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.809
or denying the Holocaust comes up.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.078
You've got to be absolutely clear

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:26.312
in your communication

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.682
that this is not acceptable dogma is not

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.284
acceptable, conversation

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.685
is not acceptable history.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.154
And you have to disavow it.

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.288
It is as simple as that.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.122
And I'm very proud

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:38.658
of the Republican Jewish Coalition

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.060
The former ambassador,

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:41.461
U.S.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.463
ambassador in the Trump administration

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:45.398
to Israel has condemned this.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.333
And so what

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.601
Donald Trump did

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.403
and his failure to condemn

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:54.607
it is really the minority of the party.

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:56.342
It's the extreme side of it.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:56.809
And that's

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:57.377
what you've got

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.878
to distance yourself from.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:01.181
And and he failed to do that.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:04.517
You told CNN you are very seriously

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.452
looking at running for president

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.554
in 20, 24.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:08.521
You're going to give a speech

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.223
this week at the Reagan Library.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.691
And I want to show our viewers

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.993
an excerpt of what you plan to say about

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:14.894
why Republicans

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.763
didn't do as well as they had

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.631
hoped in the midterm

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.099
Here's a quote from the speech

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:20.466
you'll give.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.768
Historically, Republicans

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:24.170
do not attack America's democracy.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.805
Republicans do not denigrate

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.273
our political system.

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.576
Republicans do not undermine confidence

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:30.243
in America.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.178
And Republicans do not attack

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.479
those institutions

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:36.182
that are fundamental to the rule of law.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.251
What makes you think your party is

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.219
ready to hear that now?

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:44.457
Well, what preceded that quote?

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.959
And that's absolutely

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.860
what I intend to say

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.229
in part of my remarks

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.997
to the Reagan Institute

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:52.498
but I also pointed out

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:55.301
that this last midterm elections,

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.438
the we had a red wave in Iowa.

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.473
We had a red wave in Arkansas.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.475
It was just individual candidates

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.245
that were disavowed and lost.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:06.746
And those were those

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:09.382
that did what I just recited.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.750
They didn't do

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.819
stick with Republican principles there.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.821
They got into election

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:17.323
denying and undermining the democracy.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:17.790
And they

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.425
and they're held accountable for that.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.594
That's that's okay.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.796
But we did have an election

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.698
in which Republican principles

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:26.899
were not disavowed.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:28.735
Republican principles didn't lose.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:29.102
In fact,

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:30.236
they were embrace

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.438
It is just that individual candidates

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:33.606
that strayed from those.

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.274
And so

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.208
the Republican Party

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:36.342
is in a good position

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.278
coming out of the midterm elections.

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:41.080
Not one incumbent Republican governor

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.482
lost it

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:43.983
as they ran for reelection

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.084
this last time.

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.686
These are good signs for the party.

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.521
Let's just stick with the principles.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:49.956
I'm delighted to say

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.225
Ronald Reagan set a good example for us,

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:54.127
and I'm looking forward

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.261
to making those remarks

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.896
at the Reagan Institute this week.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:59.032
Many of your potential 20, 24

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.801
rivals were once staunch Trump allies.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.336
People like Mike Pence, of course,

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:04.203
is Vice President.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.572
Mike Pompeo is Secretary of State.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.641
Chris Christie. Nikki Haley.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.443
What's your reaction to seeing them now

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.512
criticizing Trump,

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:14.080
trying to position themselves

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.815
as Trump alternatives?

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.151
You I just want to say that you have

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.752
positioned yourself like that

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.721
pretty much from from the start

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.056
coming on the show many times

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:26.826
Well, I think it is the

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:27.960
right thing to do.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.264
And it is to me predictable that

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:36.469
in what we need as as you see the party

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:39.372
moving away from Donald Trump, as you see

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.341
as understanding

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:43.576
the cost of the last midterm election,

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:45.645
that we can't have candidates

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:47.914
that win a primary but lose in November.

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:49.182
You can't have a candidate

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:52.051
that can't attract suburban voters

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:53.953
and independents

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.922
and so everyone is recognize that.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:56.356
Not so.

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:59.525
I applaud the Vice President Pence of

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:01.594
the others

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.062
that you mentioned, Chris Christie,

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.330
that's been very outspoken

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.632
we need more of those voices, not fewer.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:09.001
And I expect those voices to increase.

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:12.839
And it shouldn't be in harsh terms, tone.

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:14.507
It should be in our

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:15.942
voice of reality

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:17.143
that this is exactly

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.511
where we are as a party

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:19.112
and where

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.880
we need to go to reach out

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.014
to those independents

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.850
and expand the base of the party

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:26.686
and move beyond the Trump era.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.621
Governor, after five

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:31.824
people were killed at an LGBTQ nightclub

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:33.059
in Colorado last week,

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.627
you urged your fellow Republicans

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.629
to tone down the rhetoric,

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.698
particularly towards the trans community.

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:40.433
But just days after that

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:41.401
shooting, Georgia

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:42.702
Republican Senate candidate

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:43.836
Herschel Walker

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.671
debuted this ad

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:46.472
I want to play,

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:48.841
and it targets transgender athletes

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.178
for more than a decade,

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:54.080
I worked so hard for

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.282
I am practices to be the best.

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:57.383
But my senior year,

00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:58.484
I was forced to compete

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.319
against a biological male

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.255
that's unfair and wrong.

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:03.122
A man won

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:03.756
the swimming title

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:05.158
that belonged to a woman,

00:07:05.158 --> 00:07:05.725
and Senator

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:08.728
Warnock voted to let it happen.

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:09.429
Are you comfortable

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:11.964
with what Walker is doing there?

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:13.900
I am.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.334
I signed a law in Arkansas

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.303
that prohibited biological males

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:19.238
from competing with women

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:21.073
and women's sports.

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:22.675
To me, it's about the tone

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:24.744
and about the broader arena.

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:27.313
We also passed a hate law in Arkansas.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.750
We shouldn't be targeting

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.585
anyone because of their race

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:34.053
or their gender.

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.421
We also have to speak

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:37.457
in a compassionate way and

00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:39.892
and to have an understanding heart.

00:07:40.226 --> 00:07:42.595
And so these are difficult issues

00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:43.663
that we're dealing

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:44.997
with as a society,

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:47.700
and it's fair to debate and discuss.

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:49.702
But what about the timing has said

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:53.739
that that's

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:54.640
a fair question,

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.843
but it happens to be in the middle

00:07:56.843 --> 00:07:57.810
of an election

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.045
and you can't hardly

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:00.847
pull everything down.

00:08:00.847 --> 00:08:02.348
That's that's a fair question.

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:04.951
But the substantive issue is one

00:08:04.951 --> 00:08:07.186
that's on the hearts and minds of people.

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:08.221
And you've got to be able

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:08.955
to talk about it,

00:08:08.955 --> 00:08:10.623
state your position on it,

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:11.958
and you've got to recognize

00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:13.192
that these sensitive issues

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:13.860
have to be dealt

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.229
with by parents, by school officials,

00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:18.931
by employers as well.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:21.000
And what happened in that nightclub

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.902
is a human tragedy.

00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:24.737
And we all have to be able

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:25.605
to express

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:26.973
ourselves with compassion

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:29.108
toward that understanding.

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:31.978
And we need to work through this

00:08:31.978 --> 00:08:33.813
as a society.

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:36.249
These are challenging issues.

00:08:36.249 --> 00:08:39.085
And what happened is just simply wrong.

